Temperature (T) = 0.7 was chosen for the generator LLM as initial default to strike a balance between diversity and determinism in sampled outputs. Subsequent sensitivity analysis shown in Table~\ref{tab:temperature_sensitivity} shows that temperature does not significantly affect Edge F1: ANOVA $F(4,40) = 0.035$, $p = 0.998$, $\eta^2 = 0.004$ (negligible effect). Shapiro-Wilk normality and Levene's homogeneity assumptions were satisfied (all $p > .05$); Kruskal-Wallis yields the same conclusion. Temperature does not significantly affect Edge F1 ($p > 0.05$), justifying T=0.7 as a reasonable default.



