The right plot of Figure \ref{fig:rq1a_gt_correctness_row1} shows the aggregate performance by prompt across all CLD's and all runs showing that while Mechanistic prompt achieves the highest F1 score, and ROC-AUC, the confidence intervals still overlap at this aggregation level, showing no significantly better performance. Without the social norms CLD, the difference would likely be significant. Precision and Recall are also markedly the highest for Mechanistic prompt, with CoT being middle of the pack and the lowest for Baseline, although the differences are small and CI's overlap.	


