This experiment was added to find out in a case where a perfect retrieval quality is assumed, we still find low judge scores for certified gold standard ground truth edges.
If so, this would point toward evidence quality evaluated lower, and the low scores are not due to a retrieval artifact.

This argument can of course only be made if Judges were found to correlate with expert judgment, which we did in RQ1a: Human Validation of LLM Citation Judges which will be covered next.

